Subject: Two-way property-read PIC with promotion

What this does
  Two-way property-read PIC with promotion.

Why we need it
  A read site is one cached entry, and after 8 misses it goes dead and every read takes the ~68-instruction out-of-line lookup even at 98 % monomorphism; read sites are strongly bimorphic, so two ways cover 99.99 % of traffic.

What it adds
  Allocate the register PIC and holders at `2 * regvm_pic_count` (`pic[site]` primary unchanged, secondary at `regvm_pic_count + site`, lazily filled); `regvm_pic_fill` installs the second shape in the secondary when the primary differs, leaving the primary alive; `regvm_get_field_ic` probes the secondary before the engine lookup and, on each hit, charges one promotion credit to the primary's `misses`; at 16 credits the two ways and holders swap, so the dominant shape gets the 22-instruction inline hit (the swap is safe because every threaded caller requickens from `pic[site].kind` after the call); free, GC mark and memory accounting walk `2 * count`; put sites use primary indices only.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
